---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
---

<PageLayout meta={{ title: "Pencil: AI Ad Infrastructure & Data Layer — Kiran S Baliga" }}>
	<article class="pt-2 pb-10 sm:pt-4 sm:pb-14">
		<a
			class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 font-sans text-xs text-[#797974] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200 mb-6"
			href="/#work"
		>
			&larr; Back to selected work
		</a>

		{/* Article Header */}
		<header class="mb-8">
			<span class="block font-sans text-xs text-[#797974] mb-2">
				Pencil &middot; Engineering case study
			</span>

			<h1 class="font-sans text-[26px] sm:text-[28px] leading-[1.25] font-normal text-[#262625] mb-3">
				A more dependable foundation for AI-powered advertising.
			</h1>

			<p class="font-sans text-[14.5px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441] max-w-2xl mb-6">
				At Pencil, I worked on the infrastructure behind the creative workflow: how tenant data is accessed, how permissions compose, and how an ad report becomes a PDF.
			</p>

			{/* Role & Context Box */}
			<div class="border-y border-[#deded8] py-4">
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-2.5">
					<div>
						<span class="block font-sans text-[13.5px] font-medium text-[#262625]">
							Associate Software Engineer
						</span>
						<span class="font-sans text-[12.5px] text-[#797974]">
							KeyValue Software Systems &middot; Client engagement: Pencil
						</span>
					</div>
					<div class="sm:text-right">
						<span class="block font-sans text-[12.5px] text-[#797974] tabular-nums">
							Sep 2023&ndash;Feb 2026
						</span>
						<a
							class="font-sans text-[13px] text-[#262625] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200"
							href="https://trypencil.com"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>
							trypencil.com &nearr;
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="font-mono text-[11.5px] text-[#797974] leading-relaxed">
					Node.js &middot; Python &middot; Google Cloud SQL &middot; Custom ORM &middot; Puppeteer &middot; Docker
				</p>
			</div>
		</header>

		{/* Context */}
		<section class="space-y-3 mb-8">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[16px] font-medium text-[#262625]">
				The context
			</h2>
			<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] sm:text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441]">
				Pencil is a B2B AI ad platform for agencies working across Google, Meta, TikTok and LinkedIn. Underneath those workflows, data access and document exports had to remain predictable as tenant-specific requirements grew.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] sm:text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441]">
				The work wasn’t a wholesale rewrite. It was a series of changes to make the existing platform faster and safer to evolve: fewer expensive joins, consistent tenant boundaries, flexible custom fields and a rendering pipeline we could control.
			</p>
		</section>

		{/* Tenant Boundaries */}
		<section class="border-t border-[#deded8] pt-6 mb-8 space-y-3.5">
			<span class="font-mono text-xs text-[#797974] uppercase tracking-wider block">
				Architecture 01
			</span>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-[18px] sm:text-[20px] font-medium text-[#262625]">
				Put tenant boundaries in the data layer
			</h2>

			<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] sm:text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441]">
				I built a custom ORM / data-access layer across Node.js and Python, with automatic tenant scoping and soft-delete enforcement. These rules became infrastructure, rather than conditions every caller had to remember.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] sm:text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441]">
				We reduced costly joins around real read workloads. Metadata-driven custom fields allowed the model to vary by tenant, while fine-grained RBAC supported composable AND / OR permissions instead of a growing set of one-off checks.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] sm:text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441]">
				Cloud SQL migrations were rolled out incrementally. I coordinated the migration and downtime with the lead, using tenant-level feature flags to control the transition rather than switching every customer at once.
			</p>

			<div class="border-l-2 border-[#16a34a] pl-4 py-1.5 my-3">
				<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] font-medium text-[#262625]">
					Result: 30% faster API responses. The lesson was to optimize for the queries the product actually makes, not an idealized model.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* Document Rendering */}
		<section class="border-t border-[#deded8] pt-6 mb-8 space-y-3.5">
			<span class="font-mono text-xs text-[#797974] uppercase tracking-wider block">
				Architecture 02
			</span>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-[18px] sm:text-[20px] font-medium text-[#262625]">
				Move document rendering out of the browser
			</h2>

			<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] sm:text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441]">
				Exporting an ad report was originally tied to the client session: React rendered the page, a client-side library walked the DOM, and the browser generated a PDF on the fly. That worked for a single user looking at a simple table. It didn’t work for high-resolution proofs, large datasets, or scheduled batch exports.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] sm:text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441]">
				I rebuilt the export pipeline as a standalone service running headless Puppeteer in a containerized worker pool. Templates were isolated from the web app, and assets were pre-warmed so exports could scale independently of the interactive UI.
			</p>

			{/* Pipeline Comparison Card */}
			<div class="relative bg-[#fcfbf9] border border-[#deded8] rounded p-5 my-4">
				<div class="space-y-4">
					<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline gap-2 sm:gap-4">
						<span class="font-mono text-xs text-[#797974] w-16 uppercase">BEFORE</span>
						<span class="font-sans text-[13.5px] text-[#444441]">
							Browser UI &rarr; react-to-pdf &rarr; Download
						</span>
					</div>
					<div class="border-t border-[#deded8]"></div>
					<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline gap-2 sm:gap-4">
						<span class="font-mono text-xs text-[#797974] w-16 uppercase">AFTER</span>
						<div>
							<span class="font-sans text-[13.5px] font-medium text-[#262625] block">
								Export request &rarr; Sandboxed Puppeteer worker &rarr; PDF
							</span>
							<span class="font-sans text-xs text-[#797974]">
								Preloaded fonts + cache + print CSS
							</span>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="hidden sm:block absolute -right-2 -top-5 select-none">
					<span class="font-handwriting text-xl text-[#16a34a] rotate-[-3deg] block">
						control the whole render
					</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* Quantified Impact */}
		<section class="border-t border-[#deded8] pt-6 mb-8">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[16px] font-medium text-[#262625] mb-4">
				What changed
			</h2>

			<div class="space-y-3.5">
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-3">
					<span class="font-sans text-[18px] sm:text-[20px] font-medium text-[#16a34a] w-32 shrink-0">
						65%
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] text-[#444441]">
						Reduction in PDF rendering processing time.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-3">
					<span class="font-sans text-[18px] sm:text-[20px] font-medium text-[#262625] w-32 shrink-0">
						~1.5 sec
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] text-[#444441]">
						Click-to-PDF download time.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-3">
					<span class="font-sans text-[18px] sm:text-[20px] font-medium text-[#262625] w-32 shrink-0">
						30&ndash;40%
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] text-[#444441]">
						Reduction in end-to-end export pipeline latency &mdash; a separate measure from rendering processing time.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-3">
					<span class="font-sans text-[18px] sm:text-[20px] font-medium text-[#262625] w-32 shrink-0">
						30%
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] text-[#444441]">
						Faster API responses with query-level optimization and automated tenant scoping.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* What I'd carry into the next system */}
		<section class="border-t border-[#deded8] pt-6 mb-8 space-y-3">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[16px] font-medium text-[#262625]">
				What I’d carry into the next system
			</h2>
			<ul class="space-y-2 text-[13.5px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441] list-disc list-inside">
				<li><strong class="text-[#262625]">Design around real reads:</strong> A cleaner abstraction is only useful if it serves the workloads people depend on.</li>
				<li><strong class="text-[#262625]">Make the safe path the default:</strong> Tenant scoping and deletion rules should be embedded in the infrastructure, not scattered across application code.</li>
				<li><strong class="text-[#262625]">Own the rendering environment:</strong> A document is an output with its own requirements; it shouldn’t be an accidental screenshot of the UI.</li>
				<li><strong class="text-[#262625]">Modernize incrementally:</strong> Migrations and tenant-level flags let us improve the system without treating every change as a big-bang replacement.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		{/* Navigation Footer */}
		<div class="border-t border-[#deded8] pt-6">
			<div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-2">
				<span class="font-sans text-xs text-[#797974]">Next case study</span>
				<a
					class="font-sans text-[13.5px] text-[#262625] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200"
					href="/work/siren/"
				>
					Siren &mdash; AI communications &amp; MCP &rarr;
				</a>
			</div>
			<p class="font-sans text-[13px] text-[#797974] mt-3">
				Working through a similar engineering problem? <a class="underline hover:text-accent text-[#262625]" href="mailto:kiransbaliga@gmail.com">Let’s talk about it.</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</PageLayout>
